[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186054676,
      "id": "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a",
      "title": "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ec2482f0-18f6-5734-ab4b-55a9e398ab04",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186054676/assets/1f86b1fae6e19d108c8f128b2418fb8ee3629e21eaf3c03d8ef690af79ff7554.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+1$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,4)$, $B(-2,-2)$, $C(2,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x+1 \\\\ (4) &= 3(0)+1 \\\\ 4 &= 1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x+1 \\\\ (-2) &= 3(-2)+1 \\\\ -2 &= -5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x+1 \\\\ (7) &= 3(2)+1 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4e9ec5c2-fa84-5904-b8dc-0fae4efce5bd",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "dce5cc41-fc40-5a29-a535-6d517215c450",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$A$ and $C$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "445b137b-3781-56ba-9eca-c390e68a8817",
