    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3f3af09e-494d-5093-9553-ecec6aa93fd2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186054676/assets/3c74248b1b4cdd2a4b18625c8da0efaeecb16fe95a434cae2c496d0803806ffd.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+4$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,5)$, $B(2,6)$, $C(-2,1)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+4 \\\\ (5) &= (-1)+4 \\\\ 5 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+4 \\\\ (6) &= (2)+4 \\\\ 6 &= 6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-2,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+4 \\\\ (1) &= (-2)+4 \\\\ 1 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e0db927c-701d-5b98-bb4e-32aee46f0705",
