      ":question/id": "445a4677-c21d-564f-9eef-ec09a0be7f9e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186054676/assets/fe9dcd46524755b20c50c052540a2c177451093261d4a48cc4ce75d35dc95504.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+5$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,7)$, $B(2,7)$, $C(-1,4)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (7) &= (0)+5 \\\\ 7 &= 5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (7) &= (2)+5 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-1,4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (4) &= (-1)+5 \\\\ 4 &= 4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "393cdae8-bbc7-5c47-bf68-a1c99e01f19d",
